# Runs the support-flag probe on python: the one target CI can execute that has
# UDP but no CSPRNG, which is the combination where a support flag can lie.
#
# StunClient.isSupported must not say true there while the first line of
# discover() throws (the bug class DatagramSocket.isSupported documents).
# This is a run step rather than an assertion in a suite because every
# suite CI runs has a CSPRNG, so on those targets the invariant cannot fail
# and a test of it would be a vacuous control.
#
# Run it with `python export/python-support/flagprobe.py` once built.
-cp src
-cp tests/support
-main FlagProbe
-python export/python-support/flagprobe.py
